From 49eb47111c8e64f295509ea7cb42ba4d954fa9d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:08:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: ipq50xx: drop the NSS bring-up debug aids

Revert 5d86c24df4 ("qualcommax: ipq50xx: debug aids for NSS bring-up
work") for the RD03v2 v2 build, as its own message asks for a build
meant to be deployed: no serial sysrq, no /dev/mem, and STRICT_DEVMEM
back to the default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/config-default | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/config-default b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/config-default
index 0517c1beb5..9485b2bf88 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/config-default
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/config-default
@@ -34,7 +34,3 @@ CONFIG_QCOM_TMEL_QMP_MAILBOX=y
 CONFIG_SPI_QPIC_SNAND=y
 CONFIG_STMMAC_ETH=y
 CONFIG_STMMAC_PLATFORM=y
-CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ_SERIAL=y
-CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ_DEFAULT_ENABLE=0x1b6
-CONFIG_DEVMEM=y
-# CONFIG_STRICT_DEVMEM is not set
-- 
2.47.3

